<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Niccolò I Gattilusio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1409</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Niccolò I <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gattilusio">Gattilusio</a> was a Genoese lord of Ainos (Enez) at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maritsa">Maritsa</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>. A brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-i-gattilusio">Francesco I Gattilusio</a>, lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a>, he took control of Ainos around 1384 and also acted as regent on Lesbos. He founded the branch of the family that held Ainos as Byzantine and then Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> until 1456.</p></div>
